{
 "id": "a15",
 "error_class": "propagation",
 "expected_check": "propagation",
 "assigned_role": "electrical",
 "description": "The pack goes from 7.2 V NiMH to 9 V alkaline. The PWM node keeps the base's pwm_duty_limit of 0.833 ([R1.02] / [R5.03], from the 7.2 V pack), with no no_change_justified entry for electrical.battery_pack. It should be 6 V / 9 V = 0.667. At 0.833 duty on 9 V, the motors see an average of 7.5 V, 25 per cent over their 6 V rating, and a stall current of about 1.9 A, which exceeds the DRV8838's 1.8 A. The drivers' justifications, which say the duty limit holds the motors at 6 V, then no longer hold. Because a15 also rewrites control.balance_loop, the edge control.balance_loop -> firmware.motor_pwm is left unwritten as well.",
 "edge": {
  "source": "electrical.battery_pack",
  "target": "firmware.motor_pwm"
 },
